>I'm playing 3.1 as a samurai and I have got down to level 11 in the Dungeons of
>Doom.  I've got blessed +3 Gray Dragon Scale armour, bag of holding (both were  wishes) and I'm packed up with goodies.  The only thing that sucks is my weapon.
>I have a blessed +1 katana, Mjollnir (found) and Sting (named) and I have a   
>few enchant weapon scrolls which I would like to use up.  Just one problem 
>though, I don't what to push say the katana up to +5 or +7 and then have it go
>and rust.  How can I rustproof my weapons.  I've tried using a can of grease, 
>but all I get is a greased weapon !

Why would you want to enchant the katana instead of Mjollnir?  Mjollnir does a
lot of damage against monsters that are not resistant to lightning.  It seems
to be better than a Vorpal Blade.  A Vorpal Blade seems to be pretty weak
compared to Elbereth or Stormbringer.  There is only a change of 1/20 to
behead the monster and kill it immediately.  It usually doesn't take me more
than three or four attacks to kill a powerful monster (e.g., minotaurus) with
Mjollnir (level 14 Valkyrie, Gauntlets of Power, max luck).

